# Dependencies and compiler state
node_modules/
.build-cache/
*.tsbuildinfo
# The packed toolchain this workspace installs from. It is delivered material,
# not authored work, and it is large: the platform package alone is ~47 MB, so
# committing it puts those bytes in the baseline, in every checkpoint snapshot
# that copies and hashes the workspace, and in the `.git` tree holding both.
.benchmark-deps/
# ttsc extracts its platform package here when it repairs a missing native
# binary. One cell of eight hit it, most likely install contention while eight
# workspaces pulled the same 47 MB archive at once. It is 3.7k extracted files
# of compiler, so counting it as authored work misreports the cell by two
# orders of magnitude, and committing it would put it in the retained record.
.ttsc-repair-*/
# Nestia writes its debug dump and a per-process runtime scratch file into the
# package it is generating from. Both are tooling output: the dump landed 420
# files and 110k lines in one measured tree, counted as authored work, and the
# scratch file lives for milliseconds and lost a race with the dashboard.
packages/*/.nestia-debug-out/
.nestia.runtime.*.json

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Package outputs
packages/api/lib/
packages/backend/bin/
packages/backend/lib/
packages/backend/src/prisma/
packages/frontend/dist/

# Local SQLite state
packages/backend/prisma/db.sqlite
packages/backend/prisma/db.sqlite-journal
packages/backend/prisma/db.sqlite-shm
packages/backend/prisma/db.sqlite-wal

# Browser diagnostics
packages/frontend/playwright-report/
packages/frontend/test-results/

# Process output. A watcher or dev server redirected to a file is tooling
# noise, not authored work, and counting it as a source change misreports how
# much of the product exists.
*.log
